<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canute VI of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1163–1202</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Canute VI was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> from 1182 to 1202, the son of Valdemar I. With his adviser Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/absalon">Absalon</a> he extended Danish power along the southern Baltic, forcing the Pomeranian duke Bogislaw I to become his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> in 1185. He refused homage to Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> and was succeeded by his brother Valdemar II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canute-vi-of-denmark.jpg" alt="Canute VI of Denmark" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hideko Bondesen · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nordenskirker_Stehag(57).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
